FINAL ANSWER:
Andrew Gallant wrote most of the Rust code, but it is not only one person. Everyone else is far behind.

Figures are surviving lines at HEAD in `*.rs` files, from `git blame -w -M -C`. The scan covered 9 files and 3,303 lines, with merges excluded.

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits | Commit share |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Andrew Gallant | 2,489 | 75.4% | 128 | 67.0% |
| Inès Moreau (3 addresses, merged) | 189 | 5.7% | 3 | 1.6% |
| Sebastian Thiel | 66 | 2.0% | 1 | 0.5% |
| Ashley | 65 | 2.0% | 2 | 1.0% |
| Aron Griffis | 56 | 1.7% | 1 | 0.5% |
| Niv Kaminer | 43 | 1.3% | 2 | 1.0% |
| mcharsley | 43 | 1.3% | 1 | 0.5% |

Marvin Löbel, Martin Sehnoutka and Yufeng Wang each hold 1.1–1.2%. 31 more authors hold 7.2% together, and the largest of them is Garrett Berg at 1.0%.

**Bus factor** is the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines together reach 50% of the lines counted. It is 1: Andrew Gallant alone holds 75.4%. Two authors are enough to reach 80%. Both numbers cover all Rust files in the repo.

**Identity merge (a guess):**
- I merged Inès Moreau's three addresses into one person, based on names and addresses. Nothing was written to `.mailmap`.
- Unmerged, Inès Moreau holds 105 lines (3.2%) and "Ines Moreau" holds 84 lines (2.5%). Merged, it is 189 lines (5.7%).
- Merging puts Inès second. Without it, the second-place holder is Inès Moreau with 105 lines, and Sebastian Thiel stays third.
- Niv Kaminer and nivkner share one address, so they are counted as one person (43 lines).
- Ashley and Ashley Mannix may be the same person. The evidence is weak, so I left them separate: Ashley has 65 lines and Ashley Mannix has 4. Merged it would be 69 lines (2.1%).

**What was left out:**
- `src/ucd_tables.rs` was dropped as generated (647 lines).
- The `github-actions[bot]` account was excluded (9 lines, 1 commit). Its lines are credited to nobody.

**Checks:**
- **Copy detection:** I used `-C`. Without it, Andrew Gallant would hold 79.8% (2,635 lines) instead of 75.4%. Ashley would hold 1.1% (36 lines) instead of 2.0%. Garrett Berg would hold 0 lines instead of 33 (1.0%).
- **Mechanical rewrites:** the tool set aside none. It flagged `c584a1d` ("style: switch to rustfmt", Andrew Gallant), which I checked with `git show --stat`. It touched 9 files, mostly formatting. Excluding it with `--ignore-rev` moves Andrew Gallant to 75.1% (2,481 lines). Aron Griffis rises from 56 to 60 lines (1.8%). The ranking does not change.

Surviving lines do not measure quality, review work, or code that was deleted on purpose.
